>> title: Seaweed and Egg Drop Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: seaweed, laver, egg, cantonese, quick soup, weeknight, stovetop
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: 紫菜蛋花湯, zi coi daan faa tong, ji choi dan fa tong, seaweed and egg drop soup, laver and egg soup, nori egg soup, 滾湯, gwan tong
>> servings: 4
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: narrow — the egg goes into water that has stopped moving; into a rolling boil it shreds into cotton instead of ribbons
>> washing-up: the saucepan, a bowl to beat the eggs in
>> keeps: not at all — the egg ribbons go rubbery and the laver slumps, and it is a ten-minute soup to make again

>> step: A 滾湯: the water boils first and everything else is quick. Sesame oil goes in at the end.
A 滾湯: the water boils first and everything else is quick.

>> step: boil the water with the dried shrimp, 5 min
Boil @water{5%cups}(1.2 L) with @dried shrimp{1%Tbs}(haa mai; rinsed — a spoonful is all the savour this bowl needs) in a #saucepan{} ~boil{5%min}.

>> step: beat the eggs
Beat @eggs{2} with a fork until the white and the yolk are one colour and no further.

>> step: stir the laver in, 1 min
Stir @laver{1/3%oz}(10 g; zi coi, the sheets torn up — they melt into the broth) into @&(~2)shrimp water{} and ~stir{1%min}.

>> step: pour the egg in a thread, off the boil
Pour @&(~2)beaten egg{} into @&(~1)soup{} in a thin thread, moving your hand in a circle, with the pan off the heat and the water gone still.

>> step: finish with sesame oil
Finish @&(~1)soup{} with @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}(5 mL), @scallion{1}(sliced thin), @white pepper{1/4%tsp} and @kosher salt{3/4%tsp}.
